From: Ian Petersen <ispeters@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC: env-gated value-init of ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl trailing args

NOT FOR UPSTREAM. Mechanism knockout for the nondeterministic crash
tracked at llvm/llvm-project#191361.

ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl::CreateDeserialized sets
NumTemplateArgs immediately but leaves the trailing TemplateArgument
array as raw ASTContext bump-allocator storage. The array is written
only at the end of
ASTDeclReader::VisitImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl, by
setTemplateArguments(), after every argument has been read. Because
deserialization is re-entrant, a nested read can reach the decl in that
window via a ConceptSpecializationExpr; StmtProfiler then walks
getTemplateArguments() and dereferences whatever is in the slab.

Value-initializing under the env var turns those wild reads into Null
TemplateArguments. That is NOT a fix -- it trades a crash for a
silently incorrect FoldingSetNodeID, and therefore for potential
mis-uniquing of the FunctionProtoType being deserialized -- but it is a
clean single-variable test: the allocation size and address are
unchanged, so this arm perturbs no heap layout, unlike the constraint
cache reserve, MallocScribble and ASan arms.

Arms:
  unset                          -> stock behaviour (control)
  CLANG_ICS_INIT_TRAILING_ARGS=1 -> value-initialize the trailing array

A one-shot "[ics-init]" line on stderr proves the arm fired rather than
silently no-opping. It prints at most once per process, and stderr is
discarded by the rate-counting loops, so rates are unaffected.

NOTE: paths in this diff are relative to the `clang/` subdirectory of
the llvm-project monorepo, to match this repo's clang derivation's
sourceRoot (clang-src-.../clang).
---
diff --git a/lib/AST/DeclTemplate.cpp b/lib/AST/DeclTemplate.cpp
index 3ff6e3a..8744c85 100644
--- a/lib/AST/DeclTemplate.cpp
+++ b/lib/AST/DeclTemplate.cpp
@@ -32,7 +32,10 @@
 #include "llvm/ADT/STLExtras.h"
 #include "llvm/ADT/SmallVector.h"
 #include "llvm/Support/ErrorHandling.h"
+#include "llvm/Support/raw_ostream.h"
 #include <cassert>
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <memory>
 #include <optional>
 #include <utility>
 
@@ -1150,8 +1153,46 @@ ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl *ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl::Create(
 ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl *
 ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl::CreateDeserialized(
     const ASTContext &C, GlobalDeclID ID, unsigned NumTemplateArgs) {
-  return new (C, ID, additionalSizeToAlloc<TemplateArgument>(NumTemplateArgs))
-      ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl(EmptyShell{}, NumTemplateArgs);
+  auto *Result =
+      new (C, ID, additionalSizeToAlloc<TemplateArgument>(NumTemplateArgs))
+          ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl(EmptyShell{}, NumTemplateArgs);
+
+  // DIAGNOSTIC HOOK (downstream patch, not for upstream).
+  //
+  // The trailing TemplateArgument array is left as raw storage here; it is
+  // only written later, by ASTDeclReader::VisitImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl
+  // calling setTemplateArguments() *after* it has finished reading every
+  // argument. NumTemplateArgs, however, is set right now. Between the two
+  // points the decl claims to have N arguments while the array holds whatever
+  // the ASTContext bump slab happened to contain, and deserialization is
+  // re-entrant: a nested read can reach this decl through a
+  // ConceptSpecializationExpr and hand the array to StmtProfiler, which reads
+  // every element's kind and then its payload.
+  //
+  // Value-initializing here does not fix that -- it converts a wild read into
+  // a Null TemplateArgument, i.e. a crash into a silently wrong
+  // FoldingSetNodeID -- but it is a mechanism-specific knockout: the
+  // allocation size and address are unchanged, so unlike every previous
+  // suppressor this one perturbs no heap layout at all.
+  //
+  //   unset                          -> stock behaviour (control)
+  //   CLANG_ICS_INIT_TRAILING_ARGS=1 -> value-initialize the trailing array
+  //
+  // The one-shot stderr note exists so the arm cannot silently no-op; it
+  // fires at most once per process and goes to stderr, so rate-counting
+  // loops that discard stderr are unaffected.
+  if (std::getenv("CLANG_ICS_INIT_TRAILING_ARGS")) {
+    std::uninitialized_value_construct_n(Result->getTrailingObjects(),
+                                         NumTemplateArgs);
+    static bool Reported = false;
+    if (!Reported) {
+      Reported = true;
+      llvm::errs() << "[ics-init] value-initializing trailing "
+                      "TemplateArgument arrays\n";
+    }
+  }
+
+  return Result;
 }
 
 void ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl::setTemplateArguments(
-- 
2.43.0
